  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> be a quadrilateral in which <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is perpendicular to <math><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math> and <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The area of the quadrilateral <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;sq. units. The diameter (in units) of a circle touching all the sides of the quadrilateral is",
